<title>ABU DHABI: OPEC should try to keep strong oil market - Rakad.</title>
<headline>OPEC should try to keep strong oil market - Rakad.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC President and United Arab Emirates acting Oil Minister Rakad bin Salem bin Rakad said on Monday that OPEC ministers meeting in November should work towards maintaining the current strong oil market.</p>
<p>The minister, who was attending a gas conference, stopped short of saying whether the UAE supported a change in the group's output ceiling.</p>
<p>&quot;We will get the views and exchange opinions in the best (way) to maintain the present situation,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The ceilings are another matter. According to every OPEC member we will discuss it,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Rakad also said that the return of Iraqi oil to the market would not hurt prices.</p>
<p>&quot;(OPEC) has done everything for Iraq...Their quota is already included,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Oil prices are currently at five-year highs.</p>
</text>
